{
  "source": "HYBRID bake: HEAD (rows 0-11, the hat/face/upper-torso) kept EXACTLY as baked from the original walk-up-cycle.svg (the whole-frame, no-group-split reference every prior walkUp.json came from) -- untouched by this update. BODY (rows 12-19, legs + lower torso) replaced with the new walk-up-cycle.svg's <g style=\"animation: upbody0..3 ...\"> groups, per the user's explicit \"replace only the body part\" request: that file also has a separate always-visible \"uphead\" group with its own bob keyframe, which was deliberately NOT used here, so the head keeps its original (non-bobbing) motion and only the legs/lower-body pose changes per frame. The new file draws a brown bag-strap diagonally across the back in the upbody groups, at the same columns in all four frames, so it stays on one consistent side throughout the cycle -- reproduced verbatim, unmirrored. Row 12 (the collar seam) comes from the new file's body groups, which all draw an identical collar line there matching its own \"uphead\" group's matching duplicate row, so the seam against the kept head is a shared, non-animated row. Colours re-clustered from scratch across BOTH the kept head pixels and the new body pixels together, down to 40 keys (custom JS k-means++, no deps, same seeded PRNG as every other bake) from 174 combined near-unique source hexes -- so the palette keys/letters here do NOT correspond 1:1 with the previous walkUp.json's palette. Every column doubled for this game's non-square ~1.667:1 character cell, same as every other sprite in this project.",
